{
  "concept": "Every feature of a parabola — vertex, axis of symmetry, intercepts — is determined by its equation, so moving the vertex moves the symmetry line and changing the vertical stretch respaces the intercepts.",
  "figureType": "line_plot",
  "elements": [
    "x-axis and y-axis, each numbered -6 to 6, with dotted gray gridlines at integer values",
    "axis labels 'x' at right end of horizontal axis and 'y' at top of vertical axis",
    "teal upward-opening parabola y = (x - 1)^2 - 4 with arrowheads on both rising branches",
    "red dashed vertical axis of symmetry at x = 1, with label 'Axis of symmetry' and pointer arrow",
    "black dot at the vertex (1, -4), with label 'Vertex' and pointer arrow",
    "black dots at the x-intercepts (-1, 0) and (3, 0), with label 'x-intercepts' and pointer arrows",
    "black dot at the y-intercept (0, -3), with label 'y-intercept' and pointer arrow",
    "black dot at the mirror partner of the y-intercept (2, -3)"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "dragVertex",
      "type": "drag",
      "teaches": "The vertex is the anchor of the parabola: dragging it moves the axis of symmetry, the intercepts, and every paired point together, showing the vertex fixes both the turning point and the symmetry line"
    },
    {
      "id": "verticalStretch",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Vertical stretch a",
      "range": [0.25, 3, 0.25],
      "default": 1,
      "teaches": "The leading coefficient controls how fast the branches rise: larger a pulls the x-intercepts closer together, smaller a spreads them apart, while the axis of symmetry and vertex stay fixed"
    },
    {
      "id": "featureHighlight",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Highlight features",
      "options": ["All labels", "Intercepts", "Symmetry markers"],
      "default": "All labels",
      "teaches": "Switching emphasis ties each vocabulary term to its visible feature: intercepts are axis crossings, and the vertex, axis line, y-intercept, and its mirror point are all reflections about the symmetry line"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Read the features",
      "narration": "The parabola y = (x − 1)² − 4 shows all key features at once: vertex at (1, −4), axis of symmetry x = 1, x-intercepts at −1 and 3, y-intercept at −3 and its mirror point at (2, −3).",
      "state": { "verticalStretch": 1, "featureHighlight": "All labels" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Check the symmetry",
      "narration": "Highlighting the symmetry markers shows the y-intercept and its mirror point sit at equal heights on opposite sides of the dashed line, equally far from x = 1 — the defining test of the axis of symmetry.",
      "state": { "verticalStretch": 1, "featureHighlight": "Symmetry markers" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Drag the vertex",
      "narration": "Drag the vertex to a new location: the dashed axis of symmetry, both intercepts, and the mirror pair all travel with it — the vertex alone determines where the symmetry line lies.",
      "state": { "verticalStretch": 1, "featureHighlight": "Symmetry markers" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Stretch the parabola",
      "narration": "Increase a and the branches steepen, pulling the x-intercepts inward toward the axis; decrease a and they spread outward. The vertex and axis of symmetry never move.",
      "state": { "verticalStretch": 2.5, "featureHighlight": "Intercepts" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The vertex determines the axis of symmetry, and the vertical stretch determines how far the x-intercepts sit from that axis — two parameters completely fix the parabola's geometry.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Coordinate plane spanning -6 to 6 on both axes with light dotted gray gridlines at integers; axes drawn as solid black lines with arrowheads. Parabola is a heavy teal curve opening upward with arrowheads at the tops of both branches, defaulting to y = (x−1)² − 4 (vertex (1,−4), x-intercepts −1 and 3, y-intercept −3, branch tops near y = 5 at x = −2 and x = 4). Red dashed vertical line through the vertex, full height of the plot. Filled black dots at vertex, both x-intercepts, y-intercept, and mirror point. Labels 'Axis of symmetry', 'x-intercepts', 'y-intercept', 'Vertex' with thin leader arrows, positioned as in the original (axis label upper right, x-intercepts label right, y-intercept and Vertex labels lower area). Dragging the vertex re-forms the curve as y = a(x−h)² + k in real time; the stretch slider changes a only. In highlight modes, non-emphasized labels and dots fade to gray while emphasized ones stay full black/red."
}

